---
// /documentation/install
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import ClickPath from '../../components/docs/ClickPath.astro';
import Note from '../../components/docs/Note.astro';
import Screenshot from '../../components/docs/Screenshot.astro';
---
<DocsLayout slug="install">
  <p class="docs-lede">Most of the 10 minutes is waiting for Salesforce.</p>

  <h2 id="install">Install from AppExchange</h2>
  <ol class="docs-steps">
    <li><div>Open the AI Assist listing on AppExchange and click <strong class="ui">Get It Now</strong>.</div></li>
    <li><div>Choose your sandbox or production org and log in.</div></li>
    <li><div>Pick <strong class="ui">Install for Admins Only</strong>. You'll give everyone else access once it's set up.</div></li>
    <li><div>Wait for the email from Salesforce saying the install finished.</div></li>
  </ol>
  <Screenshot id="install-for-admins" />

  <h2 id="automatic">What happens automatically</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You're given the <strong>AI Assist Super User</strong> permission set, so every AI Assist tab is open to you.</li>
    <li>The nightly clean-up job is scheduled. It deletes conversations past their retention date and old log entries.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="check">Check it worked</h2>
  <p>Open the App Launcher and search for <strong>AI Assist</strong>. You should see tabs including AI Agent Wizard, AI Agent Models and AI Assist Settings.</p>
  <Note type="watch" title="Can't see the app?">Assign yourself the AI Assist Super User permission set in <ClickPath steps={['Setup', 'Permission Sets']} />, then refresh the page.</Note>

  <h2 id="upgrades">Upgrades</h2>
  <p>Upgrading keeps all your settings, agents and permission set assignments. The clean-up job is checked and rescheduled if it was stopped.</p>
</DocsLayout>
